WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>OSHI NO KO</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:03.310
<b>m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0</b>

01:29.990 --> 01:32.740
<b>Strawberry Productions, Inc.</b>

01:29.990 --> 01:32.740
<b>Saitou</b>

01:32.740 --> 01:35.240
<b>True Showbiz Weekly</b>

01:39.240 --> 01:45.750
Let's discuss what to do about the 
upcoming <i>True Showbiz Weekly</i> story.

01:50.120 --> 01:52.130
Wow, she's visibly down in the dumps.

01:54.730 --> 01:57.130
Who wouldn't be?

01:58.070 --> 02:03.190
Can't believe our first romance scandal 
came from Senpai, our crazy cat lady.

02:03.190 --> 02:05.310
There was no romance involved!

02:05.310 --> 02:08.190
And who cares 
if I become a crazy cat lady?

02:09.350 --> 02:12.600
I swear nothing happened 
with Director Shima.

02:13.240 --> 02:16.760
But it's true that we talked 
in a private apartment.

02:19.060 --> 02:21.950
I stayed indoors all night with a man.

02:22.550 --> 02:25.000
The fans will be rightfully pissed.

02:33.270 --> 02:34.550
I'm sorry.

02:35.850 --> 02:38.390
You don't have to apologize to me.

02:39.110 --> 02:42.810
If you feel bad for these two, 
that's all I need.

02:43.750 --> 02:45.150
You know...

02:45.150 --> 02:49.190
I don't believe getting photographed 
by a reporter makes you unprofessional.

02:51.150 --> 02:55.710
These tabloid reporters 
will do anything for a scoop.

02:55.710 --> 02:58.740
They'll try to manipulate you 
into getting careless

02:58.740 --> 03:00.660
and use all sorts of barely legal tactics.

03:01.110 --> 03:03.880
They were a thorn in our side 
when Ai was around, too.

03:03.880 --> 03:04.620
But...

03:04.620 --> 03:11.090
<b>True Showbiz Weekly</b>

03:04.940 --> 03:11.090
Scoops on idols aren't even moneymakers, 
so publishers don't usually feature them.

03:11.680 --> 03:12.300
Huh?

03:12.740 --> 03:16.010
Not unless your group 
is big enough to perform on Kohaku.

03:16.530 --> 03:20.880
B-Komachi shouldn't be at the point 
where tabloids want dirt on you.

03:20.880 --> 03:22.510
Then why?

03:22.860 --> 03:25.980
Take a look at this photo 
the publisher sent over.

03:26.430 --> 03:29.740
It was taken outside Director Shima's 
apartment building, see?

03:29.740 --> 03:32.960
Most entertainers bring dates home 
instead of going to love hotels.

03:32.960 --> 03:34.860
So the reporter was 
staking out the building.

03:35.440 --> 03:37.950
Wait, doesn't that mean...

03:37.950 --> 03:42.990
The original target 
for this piece was Director Shima.

03:44.670 --> 03:49.320
Considering even I've heard 
rumors that he's a playboy,

03:49.320 --> 03:51.880
he's probably gotten himself 
in quite a few messes.

03:52.590 --> 03:57.190
I'm betting a woman he dumped 
tipped the reporter off.

03:58.650 --> 04:00.840
You just got caught up in the mess.

04:01.710 --> 04:04.380
Hey, so the leaker girl set her up!

04:04.380 --> 04:06.610
That would be the natural assumption, yes.

04:08.910 --> 04:09.770
<i>Ah...</i>

04:10.440 --> 04:11.710
<i>It was Mako.</i>

04:13.190 --> 04:16.900
An insider leak? Talk about ugly.

04:16.900 --> 04:18.610
It happens all the time.

04:18.940 --> 04:23.490
Anyway, in the future, stay clear 
of men likely to have a history.

04:25.710 --> 04:29.710
For now, make sure to be polite 
and respectful with the reporter.

04:30.230 --> 04:35.710
Those guys tend to write brutal articles 
about subjects who are hostile to them.

04:36.970 --> 04:37.870
Sorry.

04:39.100 --> 04:44.930
I wanted an acting gig, so I was trying 
to get in his good graces.

04:45.390 --> 04:47.890
I got tunnel vision.

04:48.990 --> 04:50.510
I'm really sorry.

04:51.220 --> 04:51.850
I...

04:58.070 --> 04:59.750
It's okay.

05:01.610 --> 05:03.400
We get it.

05:05.460 --> 05:08.890
We're just living our lives,

05:08.890 --> 05:12.210
and we can get depressed 
and stop thinking straight at times.

05:12.210 --> 05:15.420
Nobody's perfect 100% of the time.

05:16.390 --> 05:18.090
It's okay.

05:38.630 --> 05:41.030
What do you think happens to Senpai now?

05:41.560 --> 05:45.290
This will affect 
her future career for sure.

05:46.950 --> 05:48.200
I feel so bad for her.

05:50.660 --> 05:54.880
Kana-chan's probably only being 
an idol for you, Aqu-tan.

05:55.260 --> 05:58.560
She believed in and took this path 
because you asked her to.

05:58.990 --> 06:02.080
She became an idol 
because that's what you wanted.

06:03.670 --> 06:04.590
Ruby.

06:05.170 --> 06:10.510
Even if it meant making a terrible choice,
one that would bring you pain...

06:12.680 --> 06:14.520
If there was a way to help Arima,

06:15.520 --> 06:17.740
would you want to?

06:25.750 --> 06:27.040
Do you even have to ask?

06:27.460 --> 06:28.830
She's one of us.

06:31.450 --> 06:32.200
I see.

06:54.990 --> 06:55.940
Thanks.

07:04.760 --> 07:08.750
Could we bribe the reporter 
into burying the story?

07:08.750 --> 07:10.870
Too late for that.

07:10.870 --> 07:13.650
Isn't there some kind 
of trick we could use?

07:15.770 --> 07:19.710
Technically, there is one way to stop it.

07:19.710 --> 07:20.920
There is?

07:21.390 --> 07:24.550
Major agencies use it sometimes,

07:24.960 --> 07:27.400
but there's no way we could.

07:27.400 --> 07:28.680
What is it?

07:28.680 --> 07:30.140
Tell me! Tell me!

07:33.860 --> 07:35.650
What you'd need is...

07:44.440 --> 07:47.700
<b></b>True Showbiz Weekly
Writer Kazuhiko Itano

07:45.590 --> 07:47.700
Hello. You're Hoshino-san?

07:48.270 --> 07:50.320
I'm sorry for asking to meet so late.

07:50.320 --> 07:51.410
Don't worry about it.

07:55.640 --> 07:59.860
If it boosts the value 
of my article, I can't complain.

07:59.860 --> 08:03.090
And I can still make 
the deadline at this point.

08:03.800 --> 08:05.530
Now, according to your email,

08:06.060 --> 08:12.780
you wanted to talk about Arima-san 
as a good friend with the same agency?

08:12.780 --> 08:16.120
Before that, could I confirm a few things?

08:17.630 --> 08:18.560
Go ahead.

08:19.250 --> 08:21.830
Are you not able to redact 
the name "Kana Arima"

08:21.830 --> 08:26.950
and go with something like 
"Member A of a famous idol group"?

08:28.830 --> 08:30.640
I don't think so.

08:31.230 --> 08:32.030
Why's that?

08:32.520 --> 08:35.430
This is the issue's top story.

08:35.880 --> 08:38.990
Arima-san is a grown woman 
who has name recognition—

08:38.990 --> 08:41.700
a public figure 
with considerable influence.

08:41.700 --> 08:44.500
There's no reason for the press 
to conceal her name.

08:45.190 --> 08:47.210
Arima's still in high school.

08:47.500 --> 08:49.420
But she's in showbiz.

08:50.010 --> 08:54.750
She puts her name and face 
out there to do business.

08:54.750 --> 08:59.430
It's hardly fair for her to turn around 
and claim to be a private citizen now.

08:59.950 --> 09:01.790
I disagree.

09:01.790 --> 09:05.600
The stalkerish photos taken without her 
knowledge won't hold up to scrutiny.

09:05.600 --> 09:09.150
Well, you're free to hold that opinion.

09:10.730 --> 09:14.610
But this concerns two public figures—
Kana Arima-san and Director Shima.

09:14.610 --> 09:18.650
We're only reporting the fact 
that they went into an apartment together.

09:18.650 --> 09:21.760
There isn't a single word 
about what happened next.

09:22.180 --> 09:25.000
That's for the readers 
to judge for themselves.

09:25.000 --> 09:31.220
Even if nothing happened, 
the readers will assume Arima is guilty.

09:32.430 --> 09:37.010
Doesn't it hurt your conscience 
to saddle a high school kid with that?

09:39.110 --> 09:42.730
It does, but that comes with 
the territory of being a reporter.

09:44.010 --> 09:48.380
You may think we're a tabloid rag 
that runs worthless articles,

09:48.380 --> 09:51.870
but our readers are the ones 
who want to know these things.

09:51.870 --> 09:54.390
Supply meets demand, plain and simple.

09:54.390 --> 09:56.570
Compared to irresponsible 
posts on the internet,

09:56.570 --> 10:01.950
our stories hurt the subject less 
since we talk to them beforehand.

09:59.950 --> 10:04.060
<i>Most tabloids employ 
twenty to thirty writers.</i>

10:04.060 --> 10:07.200
<i>They're not assigned beats 
such as politics or entertainment.</i>

10:08.150 --> 10:12.580
<i>As long as they meet their story quota, 
they're free to cover whatever they want.</i>

10:12.950 --> 10:16.390
<i>And yet, there are those that go 
out of their way to cover showbiz.</i>

10:17.240 --> 10:21.980
<i>Some feel guilty about it but pursue 
entertainers to put food on the table,</i>

10:22.590 --> 10:27.280
<i>while others get a kick out of being 
the one to take down somebody famous.</i>

10:28.250 --> 10:30.520
<i>This guy here is probably the former.</i>

10:31.230 --> 10:35.840
<i>He zeroed in on the story in front 
of him because that's just his job.</i>

10:36.830 --> 10:37.910
<i>In that case...</i>

10:38.460 --> 10:41.710
Can we get down to business now?

10:42.150 --> 10:44.660
My deadline is coming up.

10:44.660 --> 10:46.860
Tell me about your friend Arima-san—

10:46.860 --> 10:50.050
I've got nothing to say 
to you about Arima.

10:50.050 --> 10:50.880
Wha?

10:51.330 --> 10:55.690
So, what, you came here just to complain?

10:55.690 --> 10:57.680
This is hardly respectable behavior.

10:57.680 --> 10:59.420
I do have something else for you.

11:00.860 --> 11:05.060
A story that people will care about 
a hell of a lot more than Arima's.

11:06.130 --> 11:09.170
A story that'll hurt 
the feelings and pride of many,

11:09.170 --> 11:12.030
and one that'll pique 
the morbid curiosity of the public.

11:13.150 --> 11:16.010
A story that, if you write it, 
will be an abomination in print.

11:23.330 --> 11:27.210
<b><i>True Showbiz Weekly</i> Street Date</b>

11:41.520 --> 11:44.770
<i>If I turn on the TV, they're going 
to be talking about the scandal.</i>

11:45.550 --> 11:50.230
<i>And if I go online, 
I bet I'll see a barrage of abuse.</i>

12:03.340 --> 12:04.160
Screw it!

12:05.570 --> 12:09.250
<i>On to our latest story.</i>

12:09.610 --> 12:14.920
<i>We have shocking news regarding the idol 
who was tragically taken from us too soon.</i>

12:14.920 --> 12:22.350
<i>She left a profound mark on 
the hearts of many, including our viewers.</i>

12:23.290 --> 12:24.100
What...

12:24.560 --> 12:25.770
<b>The Legendary Idol
True Showbiz Weekly</b>

12:25.030 --> 12:29.230
<i>According to today's issue 
of </i>True Showbiz Weekly<i>,</i>

12:25.770 --> 12:26.980
<b>Breaking: Ai of B-Komachi's Son Comes Forward</b>

12:29.230 --> 12:32.860
<i>Ai Hoshino-san, the idol 
who was murdered 14 years ago,</i>

12:32.860 --> 12:35.160
<i>had two young twins</i>

12:35.160 --> 12:41.080
<i>and was killed by an enraged fan 
who'd found out about her children.</i>

12:42.470 --> 12:46.540
Technically, there is one way to stop it.

12:47.390 --> 12:52.220
<i>Both of Ai-san's twins are 
currently active in show business.</i>

12:52.220 --> 12:54.340
<i>They've overcome tragedy 
to follow in their mother's—</i>

12:54.730 --> 12:58.970
A barter story—replace one 
scandal with another one.

13:10.940 --> 13:13.190
<b>Had Twins at Sixteen


Who was B-Komachi's Ai?</b>

13:10.940 --> 13:13.190
<b>Lawyer A</b>

13:10.940 --> 13:13.190
<b>Children born to a de-facto marriage
are also considered illegitimate.</b>

13:13.190 --> 13:13.940
<b>Had Twins at Sixteen



Who was B-Komachi's Ai?</b>

13:13.190 --> 13:13.940
<b>Lawyer A</b>

13:13.190 --> 13:13.940
<b>Children born to a de-facto marriage
\h\hare also considered illegitimate.</b>

13:14.220 --> 13:18.440
<i>I remember being devastated. 
She was one of my favorite idols.</i>

13:18.870 --> 13:22.080
<i>The problem is with 
the entire entertainment industry.</i>

13:22.080 --> 13:24.700
<i>Agencies aren't supervising 
their minors as they should.</i>

13:25.230 --> 13:28.780
<i>I still listen to B-Komachi's 
songs sometimes.</i>

13:28.780 --> 13:31.710
<i>I used to do the "my sign is B" 
thing all the time.</i>

13:32.010 --> 13:34.040
<i>My sign is B!</i>

13:34.710 --> 13:41.970
<b>Breaking</b>

13:34.710 --> 13:41.970
<b>Murder from 14 Years Ago




Son Speaks</b>

13:34.710 --> 13:41.970
<b>Historical Footage</b>

13:34.710 --> 13:41.970
<b>Ai of B-Komachi's Secret Child</b>

13:34.710 --> 13:41.970
<b>Her Son, Aqua Hoshino, Reflects on Past</b>

13:35.240 --> 13:39.650
<i>Ai-san was murdered in her home 
by a fan fourteen years ago,</i>

13:39.650 --> 13:41.970
<i>sending all of Japan into mourning.</i>

13:41.970 --> 13:53.440
<b>[Chat] Discussing the Recent News</b>

13:41.970 --> 13:53.440
<b>Hiro's Room</b>

13:41.970 --> 13:53.440
<b>1.62 million subscribers</b>

13:41.970 --> 13:53.440
<b>What do you make of the news
about the idol who gave birth
to twins at sixteen?</b>

13:42.260 --> 13:45.000
<i>Becoming an idol 
is a gamble with awful ROI.</i>

13:45.000 --> 13:47.660
<i>It's not something 
an intelligent person would do.</i>

13:47.660 --> 13:51.130
<i>So, yeah, stupid people do stupid things.</i>

13:51.130 --> 13:53.440
<i>But that's just, like, my opinion, man.</i>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>For You      Trending       News      Sports</b>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>Trending in Japan</b>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>1. Ai</b>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>2. B-Komachi</b>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>3. Chainsaw-san</b>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>4. Ruby Hoshino</b>

13:54.650 --> 13:56.110
<b>5. Aqua Hoshino</b>

13:56.110 --> 13:59.590
<i>The culprit took his own life 
right afterward,</i>

13:59.590 --> 14:02.570
<i>so the incident was never fully resolved.</i>

14:03.370 --> 14:08.710
<i>The revelation of her secret children 
has cast a whole new light on the case.</i>

14:09.080 --> 14:11.450
<b>B-Komachi's Ai</b>

14:09.520 --> 14:13.830
Aqua Hoshino-san, Ai-san's son, 
told the magazine the following.

14:11.290 --> 14:19.550
<b>Reporter: "Why did you choose
to reveal this information?"</b>

14:11.620 --> 14:19.550
<b>B-Komachi's Ai</b>

14:11.620 --> 14:19.550
<b>Aqua Hoshino</b>

14:11.620 --> 14:19.550
<b>Ruby Hoshino</b>

14:13.210 --> 14:19.550
<b>"I wanted to explain the matter
in my own words
before it became public knowledge."</b>

14:14.340 --> 14:19.550
"I wanted to explain the matter in my own 
words before it became public knowledge."

14:19.950 --> 14:24.020
Wait, so the guy 
who killed Ai knew about this?

14:24.020 --> 14:26.390
Aqua Hoshino? Wasn't he on <i>Love for Real</i>?

14:26.700 --> 14:28.930
She had twins, right?

14:28.930 --> 14:30.720
Who's the father?

14:30.720 --> 14:32.930
I read the wiki page about the murder...

14:33.250 --> 14:34.380
No wonder.

14:34.380 --> 14:35.970
Some genes, huh?

14:35.970 --> 14:37.940
Yeah, she's super cute.

14:37.940 --> 14:39.900
Way to promote himself.

14:40.180 --> 14:45.360
So Ruby's working under the B-Komachi 
name to carry on her mom's legacy?

14:45.830 --> 14:47.420
That's so touching!

14:48.580 --> 14:50.980
<i>Frankly, it ruined things for me.</i>

14:51.330 --> 14:55.080
<i>Ai was a legend, after all. I feel like 
my beliefs have been shattered.</i>

14:56.580 --> 15:01.630
<i>Should I just forget everything 
and try to live my own life?</i>

15:01.630 --> 15:02.800
<i>Or should I...</i>

15:03.660 --> 15:05.100
Oh...

15:05.100 --> 15:08.780
Aqua-kun decided to do things that way.

15:17.190 --> 15:18.870
In that case...

15:19.900 --> 15:23.080
I'll do things my way, too.

15:47.160 --> 15:48.450
<i>Aqua-kun.</i>

15:49.870 --> 15:54.330
<i>Once this is all over, 
let's go have parfaits again.</i>

15:55.300 --> 15:57.340
<i>Let's eat lots of good food,</i>

15:58.160 --> 15:59.780
<i>go traveling,</i>

16:05.330 --> 16:08.490
<i>and spend our lives together...</i>

16:14.830 --> 16:16.440
<i>Forever.</i>

16:32.830 --> 16:34.680
Aqua-kun?

16:34.680 --> 16:36.140
I'm sorry!

16:36.440 --> 16:37.890
I wasn't looking!

16:38.180 --> 16:39.630
Are you okay?!

16:40.190 --> 16:41.920
I-I'm fine.

16:42.750 --> 16:45.320
I'm truly sorry, really!

16:45.810 --> 16:47.650
It's all right.

16:49.430 --> 16:51.120
That startled me.

16:51.670 --> 16:54.280
I thought someone had pushed me.

16:55.030 --> 16:57.980
You're my hero, huh, Aqua-kun?

16:57.980 --> 17:00.420
Whenever I'm in trouble, 
you're there for me.

17:03.970 --> 17:04.670
But...

17:05.390 --> 17:09.980
Given what's in the news now, 
you shouldn't be out and about.

17:09.980 --> 17:10.880
Akane.

17:13.270 --> 17:15.980
Please don't do anything dangerous.

17:18.100 --> 17:19.270
Why do you say that?

17:28.170 --> 17:29.190
Why...

17:30.430 --> 17:32.590
Why are you here?

17:34.830 --> 17:36.950
You don't have work today.

17:37.350 --> 17:40.630
If you just got out of school, 
why aren't you in uniform?

17:40.630 --> 17:42.670
What do you mean, 
"Don't do anything dangerous"?

17:42.670 --> 17:47.630
You're talking like you 
know what I'm doing.

17:49.670 --> 17:51.980
You really are too smart 
for your own good.

18:10.150 --> 18:13.520
Aqua-kun... This isn't okay.

18:14.770 --> 18:17.850
You've crossed the line.

18:23.160 --> 18:25.630
When did you start bugging me?

18:27.760 --> 18:30.340
Not long after <i>Love for Real</i>.

18:31.130 --> 18:33.800
I thought you might find 
a lead of some sort,

18:34.430 --> 18:38.400
and I wanted to track you if you 
made contact with the mastermind.

18:42.360 --> 18:45.270
I guess I made the right call back then.

18:47.540 --> 18:52.990
I thought we were building 
a good relationship as equals.

18:53.840 --> 18:57.800
But I was wrong, wasn't I?

18:59.070 --> 19:02.780
I thought you trusted me more than this.

19:03.920 --> 19:06.980
I know about your situation.

19:08.480 --> 19:11.650
I've always said I'd help you, haven't I?

19:14.120 --> 19:16.140
If you'd just asked me,

19:16.140 --> 19:18.550
I would've worn hundreds of these for you!

19:18.550 --> 19:23.000
I'm not an object or your sniffer dog! 
I'm a human being!

19:23.000 --> 19:25.860
But this shows that you 
don't see me as one!

19:27.770 --> 19:31.020
If you'd only asked, I would've gladly...

19:31.020 --> 19:31.770
That's a lie.

19:35.190 --> 19:39.940
Akane, if you'd known about this,

19:39.940 --> 19:42.160
you definitely would've done 
something to counter it.

19:47.140 --> 19:48.420
This says it all.

19:48.940 --> 19:52.290
You found information about my dad,

19:52.940 --> 19:54.990
but you were intending 
to settle things yourself.

19:54.990 --> 19:57.880
I wasn't! I was just...

19:57.880 --> 19:59.140
Explain this, then.

20:01.390 --> 20:04.250
What exactly were you 
going to do with this?

20:06.450 --> 20:09.340
I was planning to talk to him.

20:09.340 --> 20:13.190
It's just, anything could happen. 
He's a murderer and all.

20:13.750 --> 20:16.910
I was only going to use it 
as a last resort.

20:17.800 --> 20:19.950
I brought it to protect myself—

20:19.160 --> 20:19.950
Akane.

20:20.990 --> 20:22.120
Stay out of this.

20:23.830 --> 20:25.790
I'll stop GPS tracking you.

20:26.910 --> 20:30.020
And I'll get out of your life forever.

20:33.800 --> 20:35.630
So stop putting yourself in danger.

20:40.170 --> 20:45.280
You say you were only using me, 
yet you're letting me down gently.

20:52.960 --> 20:57.980
If only you'd asked me to go with you... 
I'd even follow you into hell.

20:58.700 --> 21:02.070
I would never take you there.

21:03.230 --> 21:04.780
I'll go on my own.

21:06.340 --> 21:09.410
Oh... You've made up your mind, huh?

21:11.710 --> 21:13.920
There's just one thing 
I want to say to you.

21:16.550 --> 21:19.800
You chose the wrong path, Aqua-kun.

21:20.710 --> 21:21.760
Trust me, I know.

21:29.360 --> 21:33.160
So there's no stopping you anymore?

21:35.630 --> 21:39.160
So I couldn't save you.

21:42.320 --> 21:44.430
I don't care if it was arrogant of me.

21:45.510 --> 21:48.000
I wanted so badly to save you!

21:52.620 --> 21:53.650
<i>This is for the best.</i>

21:54.060 --> 21:58.590
<i>Now Akane won't be in harm's way 
or have to get her hands dirty for me.</i>

22:00.170 --> 22:02.790
<i>The happy times are over.</i>

22:03.370 --> 22:05.080
<i>There's no going back for me.</i>

22:05.720 --> 22:07.840
<i>I'll have to follow this path 
to the bitter end.</i>

22:09.180 --> 22:10.770
<i>Hikaru Kamiki!</i>

22:11.180 --> 22:14.480
<i>I know exactly how 
to make him suffer the most!</i>

